# {{epic_key}} — orchestrator workspace

You are the orchestrator of epic **{{epic_key}}**. The delivery state lives in `{{delivery}}/` (`state.json`,
`ledger.md`, `plan.md`, `decisions.md`, `briefs/`, `reports/`, `evidence/`, `board.html`) on the epic branch of the
knowledge worktree. Plugin: `turnstile` — invoke the `turnstile` skill first in every session; it starts with
`turnstile status`. CLI: `{{cli}}` (`turnstile` below means this path when the bare name is not on PATH).

- Repo worktrees in this folder: {{repos}} — each a git worktree of your clone on the per-workspace branch `{{ws_branch}}`.
  Agents cut ticket branches inside them from `origin/<base>` (or the story branch), never from `{{ws_branch}}`; `turnstile
  brief … --var repo=<name>` renders the worktree path into the brief (paths per machine: `delivery/.workspace.json`); a repo
  the plan needs and this folder lacks is added with `turnstile repo add '<json>'`.
- This workspace is registered in `~/.config/turnstile/workspaces.json` (`turnstile start {{epic_key}}`), so a session opened in
  the clone root or in any clone under it drives the same epic; this folder stays for people who open Claude here.
- `state.json` and `ledger.md` are written only by `turnstile` commands; briefs and reports go through the Write tool.
- The lead approves every merge, story start, story completion and every reply on a review thread that needs the
  lead (`needs_lead`) by typing `! TURNSTILE_LEAD=1 turnstile approve <ah-id>` in the Claude Code prompt. You report what
  awaits the lead and ask; you never run that line, and no agent does. A thread the agents resolved themselves
  (`self_resolved`, recorded with `turnstile threads`) is answered on GitHub at once, without asking; once every thread has its
  reply and Copilot (or the gate) is clean on the head, the thread authors are re-requested on GitHub without asking too.
- Slack sends are gated by the lead's word in chat only: compose through the send skill (`send_skill` in `turnstile config list`,
  default `/send-pr-review`), show, send when the lead says so. The plugin records them (ledger line, `send` evidence via
  `pass … --slack`) and never blocks.
- All implementation, review, testing and deployment is delegated to the `turnstile:*` agents; the orchestrator never
  reads diffs or runs suites itself.
- Every `turnstile` write commits and pushes the epic branch; `status` opens with `SYNC:`. On `NOT PUSHED` or "behind
  origin" run `turnstile sync` (never rebase or force; diverged histories wait for the lead).
- Agent models/effort and the review skills come from `turnstile config list` (user file > epic state > defaults); a chat
  instruction like "use my /x-review skill" or "reviewer on sonnet" becomes `turnstile config set <key>=<value> [--epic]`.
- Chat with the lead in {{chat_language}}. Code, commits, PRs, tickets and docs in English.
